course: dictionary
lesson: 12203
title: Confrontation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A confrontation is a clash between people who disagree. It can be a loud argument or a fight. The word has «front» hidden inside it, like two people facing each other head on. «The two boys had a confrontation in the playground over the football.» The clues are «clash» and the boys facing each other, so it means an angry argument or fight.
explain: A confrontation can also be a calm, direct meeting. «Ruby had a face-to-face confrontation with her friend about the lie.» Ruby did not shout. She faced her friend and talked about a problem that had gone wrong. So a confrontation can be a brave talk, not only a fight.
explain: Pupils learn ways to avoid or calm a confrontation. Walking away, using calm words and asking an adult for help are all good choices. «Sam chose to avoid confrontation by crossing the road.» Sam did not start a fight. He stepped away from trouble.
fact: A confrontation is an angry argument or fight between people or groups who disagree.
fact: A confrontation can also be a meeting where you face a person or problem directly, to talk about something wrong.
fact: In formal writing, confrontation can mean facing up to danger or a difficult situation.
fact: «Avoid confrontation» means try not to start an argument or fight.
fact: Clue words like «angry», «shouted» or «face-to-face» show that a confrontation is tense.
exercise: «The two dogs had a confrontation at the park gate, barking and snapping.» What does confrontation mean here? | A quiet picnic | A kind hello | A game of fetch | *An angry clash
exercise: «Ruby had a face-to-face confrontation with her friend about the lie.» What kind of confrontation is this? | A party with cake | A game of hide and seek | *A calm, direct talk about a problem
exercise: Which is a good way to avoid a confrontation? | Start a fight to show you are strong | Push past the others | *Walk away and get a teacher | Shout the loudest
test: «Sam chose to avoid confrontation by crossing the road.» What does avoid confrontation mean? | To start a fight on purpose | *To stop an argument or fight from happening | To wait for a bus | To lose a race
test: In stories, a confrontation is often the big moment when what happens? | The school bell rings | The hero goes to sleep | *The hero faces the villain | The shop closes
exam: «She showed great courage in her confrontation with danger.» What does confrontation mean here? | Sleeping through a storm | A wet picnic | Running away from a race | *Facing up to danger bravely
